{"type":"sense","headword":"serendipity","headwordNote":"独立名词，无词形变化关系","partOfSpeech":"noun","meaning":"意外发现美好事物的运气；机缘巧合；偶然的幸运发现","phonetic":"","register":"中性偏书面，常用于文学、演讲和日常感叹","usageNote":"不可数名词，通常指一种幸运的偶然性，而非具体某件东西；说“一次机缘巧合”可用 a stroke of serendipity。","exampleEnglish":"Meeting my future business partner on that delayed flight was pure serendipity.","exampleChinese":"在那趟延误的航班上遇到我未来的生意伙伴，纯属机缘巧合。"}
{"type":"sense","headword":"serendipity","headwordNote":"独立名词，无词形变化关系","partOfSpeech":"noun","meaning":"（科学研究或探索中）意外发现珍奇事物的能力或现象","phonetic":"","register":"学术、科普语境常用","usageNote":"在科学史和科研方法讨论中，常指并非刻意寻找却获得重要发现的过程。","exampleEnglish":"The discovery of penicillin is often cited as a classic example of serendipity in science.","exampleChinese":"青霉素的发现常被引为科学界机缘巧合的经典例子。"}
{"type":"usage","value":"serendipity 是不可数名词，强调“意外+美好”的双重含义，不能用来指单纯的巧合或倒霉的意外。常见句型有 It was pure serendipity that...、by serendipity、a stroke of serendipity。注意与 coincidence（中性巧合）和 luck（泛指的运气）区分：serendipity 一定带有积极、令人惊喜的结果。"}
{"type":"collocation","phrase":"pure serendipity","meaning":"纯粹的机缘巧合","exampleEnglish":"Running into her at the tiny bookshop was pure serendipity.","exampleChinese":"在那家小书店碰到她，纯属机缘巧合。"}
{"type":"collocation","phrase":"a stroke of serendipity","meaning":"一次幸运的偶然","exampleEnglish":"Winning that grant was a stroke of serendipity for the whole team.","exampleChinese":"拿到那笔经费对整个团队来说是一次幸运的偶然。"}
{"type":"collocation","phrase":"by serendipity","meaning":"凭机缘巧合地","exampleEnglish":"The two recipes were combined by serendipity, not by design.","exampleChinese":"这两道食谱是机缘巧合地结合在一起的，并非有意为之。"}
{"type":"collocation","phrase":"a moment of serendipity","meaning":"机缘巧合的一刻","exampleEnglish":"Their first conversation was a moment of serendipity that changed both their lives.","exampleChinese":"他们的第一次交谈是改变两人一生的机缘巧合时刻。"}
{"type":"collocation","phrase":"serendipity in science","meaning":"科学中的意外发现","exampleEnglish":"The professor devoted a chapter to serendipity in science.","exampleChinese":"教授用一整章讲述科学中的意外发现。"}
{"type":"wordFamily","word":"serendipitous","partOfSpeech":"adjective","meaning":"机缘巧合的；意外幸运的"}
{"type":"wordFamily","word":"serendipitously","partOfSpeech":"adverb","meaning":"机缘巧合地；意外幸运地"}
{"type":"synonym","word":"chance","difference":"chance 只表示偶然性，可好可坏；serendipity 一定指带来美好结果的偶然。"}
{"type":"synonym","word":"coincidence","difference":"coincidence 是中性的“巧合”，不含惊喜或幸运色彩；serendipity 带有明显的积极评价。"}
{"type":"synonym","word":"fluke","difference":"fluke 多指侥幸成功，语气偏口语且常含“本不该发生”的意味；serendipity 更优雅、更书面。"}
{"type":"synonym","word":"happy accident","difference":"happy accident 是口语化的同义表达，直白易懂；serendipity 更正式、更有文学感。"}
{"type":"memory","value":"源自波斯童话《锡兰三王子》（The Three Princes of Serendip），三位王子总在旅途中意外发现宝物，于是 serendipity 就表示“意外发现珍宝的好运”。"}
{"type":"mistake","value":"serendipity 是不可数名词，不说 a serendipity 或 serendipities；要表示“一次”可用 a stroke of serendipity。"}
{"type":"mistake","value":"不要用它指坏结果的意外，如车祸、误机等，那只是 accident 或 misfortune。"}
